coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder secret create [flags] <name>

  Create a secret

  Provide the secret value with --value or non-interactive stdin (pipe or
  redirect).

OPTIONS:
      --description string
          Set the secret description.

      --enabled bool (default: true)
          Whether the secret is eligible for injection. Enabled secrets need an
          allowed target; use false to store without injecting.

      --env string
          Name of the workspace environment variable that this secret will set.

      --file string
          Workspace file path for this secret. Must start with ~/ or /.
          Availability depends on deployment policy.

      --value string
          Set the secret value. For security reasons, prefer non-interactive
          stdin (pipe or redirect).

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
